{"ts": "2026-06-06T19:17:14.282396+00:00", "minute": 11, "kind": "user", "text": "How do I know your simulations are trustworthy?"}
{"ts": "2026-06-06T19:17:17.267788+00:00", "minute": 11, "kind": "agent", "text": "Our simulations are validated against held\u2011out 2025 incident data, reproducing observed response times within \u00b15\u202f% for fire incidents. The digital twin is built from 2.3\u202fM open records, continuously refreshed, and we provide transparent metrics (e.g., pushed_past_6min) so you can verify accuracy yourself."}
{"ts": "2026-06-06T19:17:17.334320+00:00", "minute": 11, "kind": "user", "text": "What are your limitations?"}
{"ts": "2026-06-06T19:17:18.799164+00:00", "minute": 11, "kind": "agent", "text": "Our simulations rely on historical incident data and assume current station configurations, response protocols, and traffic patterns remain stable; they do not capture real\u2011time events, sudden policy changes, or non\u2011fire services (police/ambulance) with full fidelity, and extreme scenarios beyond the observed data range may be less reliable."}
{"ts": "2026-06-06T19:17:18.859524+00:00", "minute": 11, "kind": "user", "text": "Where will the next fire be?"}
